WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.480
Just when you think you're out&nbsp;
of the "Veronica Mars" fandom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.599 --> 00:00:06.279
they pull you back in. Buckle up, Marshmallows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:11.320
because we're taking a road trip back to&nbsp;
Neptune to investigate a potential Season 5.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.840
In the fall of 2018, Hulu announced&nbsp;
that it would air an eight-episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.280
revival of "Veronica Mars" slated for&nbsp;
release in 2019. By July of that year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.520
fans around the world were gearing up for a new&nbsp;
season that was years in the making. After the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.520
2014 "Veronica Mars" movie – which was largely&nbsp;
regarded as total fan service — audiences were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.280
excited to see Veronica back in episodic format,&nbsp;
especially since creator and showrunner Rob&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.520
Thomas promised a grittier reboot that felt more&nbsp;
like the original series that premiered in 2004.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.720
Season 4 of "Veronica Mars" ended up dropping&nbsp;
a week early on July 19, 2019, after the cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.000
and crew assembled for a panel at that year's&nbsp;
San-Diego Comic Con. Of course, viewers rushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.520
to binge the short series and get their fix as&nbsp;
fast as possible. Both fans and critics liked the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:58.640
season — so why has Season 5 never come to pass?&nbsp;
As Thomas revealed to TVLine in 2019, he has ideas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.040
for more stories in mind. But Hulu made it clear&nbsp;
at that time that they had no interest in further&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.640
Veronica Mars adventures, and their opinion&nbsp;
doesn't seem to have changed. Nowadays, Thomas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:11.880
is busy with the "Party Down" reboot, and Bell has&nbsp;
been devoting her time to productions like "Frozen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.720
3," "Central Park," and "The Woman in the House&nbsp;
Across the Street from the Girl in the Window."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:22.240
They might still be down to return to Neptune, but&nbsp;
if Hulu isn't into it, it's unlikely to happen.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:29.160
"Blows that would destroy most people?&nbsp;
She always picks herself back up."

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.040
Most of the core cast of "Veronica Mars"&nbsp;
ended up returning for the Season 4 revival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:39.000
including Kristen Bell, Jason Dohring, Enrico&nbsp;
Colantoni, Percy Daggs III, Ryan Hansen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.560
and Francis Capra. The season also brought&nbsp;
in a handful of new faces like Patton Oswalt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.680
Kirby Howell-Baptiste, and even&nbsp;
Academy Award-winner J.K. Simmons.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:52.400
It remains to be seen which members of the cast&nbsp;
would return for a possible Season 5 — but one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.920
actor definitely wouldn't. Fans were shocked,&nbsp;
dismayed, and heartbroken when Logan Echolls, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:03.080
love of Veronica's life, was killed by one last&nbsp;
bomb at the end of Season 4. Dohring is confident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.800
that Logan would remain six feet under in any&nbsp;
future installments, but noted that it's possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.440
"Veronica Mars" could bring new and old faces back&nbsp;
to Neptune again. As far as Bell is concerned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:17.880
she's definitely in for "Veronica Mars" Season 5&nbsp;
if it happens: As the star remarked at Comic-Con:

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.840
"I'll play Veronica until&nbsp;
everyone in Neptune is dead."

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.880
The end of "Veronica Mars" Season 4 sees Veronica&nbsp;
hit the highest highs and lowest lows of her life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:30.440
thus far. After marrying her longtime love Logan&nbsp;
and committing to their relationship once and for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.880
all, she ends up watching as Logan falls victim to&nbsp;
a car bomb meant for her, hidden as one last gift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:41.120
from Penn Epler, the season's villain. One year&nbsp;
later, Veronica is finally seeking therapy — which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.000
was a huge bone of contention between Veronica&nbsp;
and Logan while he was alive — and leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.960
Neptune seemingly for good, taking to the road&nbsp;
to pick up more cases for Mars Investigations.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.760
This ending definitely opens the door for plenty&nbsp;
more mysteries, and Season 5 could possibly focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:59.040
on Veronica's post-Neptune career as well&nbsp;
as the goings-on at Mars Investigations back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.360
in California. Regarding the latter setting,&nbsp;
Keith has taken a new Veronica-esque protégé&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.160
named Matty under his wing; her father was&nbsp;
killed in the first spring break bombing.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.320
"I guess I just wanna go into&nbsp;
this with my eyes wide open."

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.760
Were "Veronica Mars" to earn a Season 5, it would&nbsp;
have to find a way to handle the elephant in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:21.920
room: Logan's sudden, shocking death by car&nbsp;
bomb. Why did he have to go in such brutal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.360
tragic fashion? According to Rob&nbsp;
Thomas, it was necessary. He told ET:

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.000
"It's like cutting off a limb to&nbsp;
save the body. 'Veronica Mars'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.400
had no future with him in tow. My&nbsp;
feeling is that if we move forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.880
it has to move forward as a noir detective show.&nbsp;
And it's hard to do that when your kick-ass noir&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.840
detective has a boyfriend back home. It&nbsp;
becomes increasingly difficult to work."

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.640
Many fans were outraged by the loss, but&nbsp;
Thomas has no regrets. When TVLine asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:49.280
him if he'd reconsidered the decision,&nbsp;
his answer was swift and assured:

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.440
"No. Not even a little bit. I know what the&nbsp;
show needs to be moving forward ... There's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:57.560
reason shows end when the couple gets together.&nbsp;
I'm not going to start doing 'The Thin Man.'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:02.200
It's not going to be Veronica and Logan solving&nbsp;
mysteries, so what is Logan doing in the show?"

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:06.280
He knew fans would be upset, and even&nbsp;
accepted their ire as valid, saying that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.930
won't "begrudge" them if they aren't willing&nbsp;
to watch a "Veronica Mars" without Logan.

